diff --git a/docs/si_s01_source_only_v2.md b/docs/si_s01_source_only_v2.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0e3ae9d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/si_s01_source_only_v2.md
@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+# SI-S01 source-only implementation contract
+
+This new namespace implements the separately adopted source-only protocol daa1d787… on top of frozen844; it grants no launch clearance. The developer runs software tests only. Old SI-E1/E2/R19 methods, synthetic gates and budgets stay unchanged.
+
+Metadata binding authenticates the original A96 reservation digest, actual five-field row schema, full task/trial identities and five-family counts. All slots have reset42/pool42/d5, original family/hash order and H50. No real-task manifest/argv is included. Synthetic fixtures have a distinct digest and evidence class; they cannot execute --live.
+
+The chain is gate → own supervised worker → new per-task/decision producer → frozen P0 parser → source collector → fsynced unit/trajectory/S5 receipts → independent raw auditor → source-only JSON/Markdown report. Only source/P0 generation and source construct/reset/step/close are admitted. Ordinary source steps after d5 stay source; there is no separate suffix, teacher, replay, train or eval driver.
+
+The real backend reuses frozen token, PEFT and UUID/ownership assertions, not the old four-call LocalInference/ledger orchestration. It verifies actual artifact/module bytes, every enabled/default/unmerged/frozen P0 layer before/during/after, complete prepared/sent IDs+mask and raw generation metadata. The one-byte context and strict own NVML PID/UID proof precede8B weights. The existing unproven host/local PID mapping remains a runtime blocker and is never normalized by this implementation.
+
+Each task uses a fresh one-game TextWorld bridge, pool42 and one reset42; only its selected game/traj files are available to discovery. The fifth actual step is followed immediately by an anchor event, before any sixth generation or source close. A valid S5 plus sixth parser-stop remains eligible. Source Y0 is sealed independently and cannot be erased by later cleanup/run failure; unexecuted YT always NA. Full96 seal precedes E/F/S necessary bounds; incomplete stages make no structural prediction.
+
+Physical unit IDs bind run/task/phase/index/kind. Load/construct/close are separately recorded with zero reset/step debit. Reset+step alone count toward4896; source generations4800/output76800/input16M/per-call8192/time4allocated-device-hours are cumulative independent caps with pre-call full reservations and unknown failed units retained. Synthetic simulated device-time is explicitly not real GPU expenditure. The independent auditor reconstructs from raw events/trajectory, not collector summaries; prior science5142/7949 remains a separate citation.
+
+The production CLI requires Python-I, exact clean source/review/proposal hashes, original metadata, runtime inputs, isolated exact environment and unique output. Preflight-only performs static binding without tokenizer/model/env construction, units or source output, and is not clearance. The two reviewed argv lists contain one literal @AUTHORIZATION_SHA256@ only as the hash-argument value; this avoids a self-referential authorization hash. At validation that slot alone is replaced by the externally supplied trusted root digest, giving exact actual argv. No other normalization is permitted. Root supplies the independent review file (SI_S01_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_V1 / PASS_SOURCE_ONLY_SOFTWARE) and fresh authorization; developer-created software review fixtures are not real acceptance.
+
+--live creates an exclusive durable adjacent launch claim before output/worker launch; it is never removed after failure. A direct worker must belong to the exact fresh-session isolated supervisor. The separate source supervisor admits at most14400seconds, reserves cleanup time, retains authentic exit/stdout/stderr, and cleans owned descendants using unchanged low-level helpers; old1800s supervisor is untouched. Allocation begins at live CLI entry, including validation/loading/waiting/cleanup. Authorization expiry can only tighten the deadline. No automatic retry or old authorization reuse exists.
+
+No teacher quality, recovery success, training recipe or learning effect is reported. Structural NO_GO and NOT_FUTILE are source supply results only. All real runtime feasibility and launch prerequisites require new exact-SHA independent review and separate root clearance. Source-only implementation cannot close a missing host namespace/ownership capability.
+
+## Separate phase authority and externally anchored audit
+
+The base authorization is PREFLIGHT_ONLY and cannot authorize --live. A successful static preflight creates a fresh, separate zero-science receipt outside source output. Live additionally needs an externally hash-bound independent SI_S01_LAUNCH_CLEARANCE_V1, bound to that exact receipt, an authentic exit0 preflight-execution receipt, source/proposal/plan/env/caps/run/UID/output, expiry, one launch and exact full argv. Its own hash has a separate single @CLEARANCE_SHA256@ argv slot, avoiding self-reference. Failed/missing preflight, mismatched context and old or missing clearance are rejected before any runtime boundary. These real files are supplied later by root; explicit software fixtures are not real clearance.
+
+The supervisor hashes launch_context before spawning and passes its hash to the authenticated worker, then records kernel PID/UID/start identity in worker_start. Live raw audit requires those external file hashes, exact authorization plan/run/caps, real allocated_devices1, the same allocation start and external worker identity. It cannot accept a header's self-asserted PID or device count. Independent offline review must obtain those hashes from the supervising execution receipts. Synthetic budget simulations may use device1 for clock tests but still report real GPU expenditure0.
+
+A returned generation is fsynced before post-resource/PEFT guards. A later failure retains raw/tokens plus the failed/open conservative reservation; observed returned boundaries are separate from completed validated units and never hidden as zero work. Normal P0 stop priority is preserved: terminal/truncated wins, full50-action nonterminal completion is horizon even if the last map is empty. An unavailable-placeholder anchor is legal only after a normal stop before5 actual actions; every source with5 or more actions requires the timely actual S5 marker.
+
+## Bounded cleanup, complete marker publication and cost endpoint
+
+Every worker wait uses the remaining absolute allocation deadline, including the post-SIGKILL reap. An unestablished exit stays null with the observed worker identity, reaping error and incomplete cleanup; elapsed time and survivors remain recorded. SIGKILL alone does not prove exit or GPU release.
+
+worker_start.json is durably written to a same-directory temporary file and published by an exclusive atomic hard link, then the directory is fsynced. The worker cannot observe a partial final marker, and publication never overwrites an existing marker. All PID/UID/start-tick/parent/context hash checks remain unchanged.
+
+Source report hours end at collector_run_closed. They are an explicitly marked stage lower bound and exclude later audit, reporting and supervisor cleanup. Only the authentic supervisor_exit allocated_device_hours is the final allocation-cost authority; the overlapping values must not be added. A source report alone supplies no final resource total or release proof.
diff --git a/scripts/run_si_s01_source_only.py b/scripts/run_si_s01_source_only.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0182465
--- /dev/null
+++ b/scripts/run_si_s01_source_only.py
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""SI-S01 source-only. No default runtime, input, output, release or automatic retry."""
+from __future__ import annotations
+import argparse,json,os,sys,time
+from pathlib import Path
+from datetime import datetime,timezone
+ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
+sys.path.insert(0,str(ROOT/'src'))
+from self_improvement.si_s01.contract import insist
+from self_improvement.si_s01.gate import authenticate,complete_preflight,source_binding
+
+def main(argv=None):
+    entered=time.monotonic()
+    parser=argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)
+    parser.add_argument('--authorization',type=Path,required=True);parser.add_argument('--authorization-sha256',required=True)
+    parser.add_argument('--proposal',type=Path,required=True)
+    modes=parser.add_mutually_exclusive_group(required=True)
+    modes.add_argument('--preflight-only',action='store_true');modes.add_argument('--live',action='store_true');modes.add_argument('--worker',action='store_true',help=argparse.SUPPRESS)
+    parser.add_argument('--clearance',type=Path);parser.add_argument('--clearance-sha256')
+    parser.add_argument('--launch-context-sha256',help=argparse.SUPPRESS)
+    args=parser.parse_args(argv)
+    try:
+        insist(sys.flags.isolated==1,'requires isolated python -I')
+        mode='preflight' if args.preflight_only else 'worker' if args.worker else 'live'
+        permit=authenticate(ROOT,args.authorization,args.authorization_sha256,args.proposal,
+            invocation=list(sys.orig_argv),mode=mode,worker=args.worker,clearance_path=args.clearance,clearance_sha256=args.clearance_sha256,launch_context_sha256=args.launch_context_sha256)
+        if args.preflight_only:
+            complete_preflight(permit)
+            print(json.dumps(dict(permit.artifact_receipt)|{'status':'STATIC_PREFLIGHT_ONLY_NOT_CLEARANCE','evidence_class':permit.plan.evidence_class,'science_output_exists':permit.output.exists()}));return 0
+        if args.worker:
+            from self_improvement.si_s01.runtime import run_worker
+            return run_worker(permit)
+        from self_improvement.si_s01.supervisor import supervise_source
+        from self_improvement.si_p3.runtime_gate import utc
+        remaining=(min(utc(permit.authorization['expires_utc']),utc(permit.clearance['expires_utc']))-datetime.now(timezone.utc)).total_seconds()
+        seconds=min(permit.ceilings['device_hours']*3600,remaining)
+        command=[sys.executable,'-I',str(Path(__file__).resolve()),'--worker','--authorization',str(args.authorization.resolve()),'--authorization-sha256',args.authorization_sha256,'--proposal',str(args.proposal.resolve()),'--clearance',str(args.clearance.resolve()),'--clearance-sha256',args.clearance_sha256]
+        context={'source_sha':permit.authorization['source_sha'],'authorization_sha256':permit.authorization_sha256,
+                 'proposal_sha256':permit.proposal_sha256,'evidence_class':permit.plan.evidence_class,'plan_sha256':permit.plan.sha256,
+                 'supervisor_argv':list(sys.orig_argv),'allocation_started_monotonic':entered,'source_binding':source_binding(permit),'clearance_sha256':permit.clearance_sha256}
+        receipt=supervise_source(command,permit.output,context=context,seconds=seconds,environment=permit.authorization['environment'])
+        return 0 if receipt['authentic_returncode']==0 and receipt['within_time_cap'] and not receipt['deadline_triggered'] and not receipt['members_after_cleanup'] else 1
+    except Exception as error:
+        print(json.dumps({'status':'REJECTED_OR_SOURCE_TECHNICAL_STOP','exception':type(error).__name__,'message':str(error),'resource_evidence':getattr(error,'resource_evidence',None)}),file=sys.stderr);return 1
+if __name__=='__main__':raise SystemExit(main())
